What do beginners usually say about it in reviews?Ask MaggieBeginners often praise the Hailey Crossbody for its convenience and style.

Crystal R. loves not needing a purse anymore, just her Bandolier.
Bridget W. appreciates the hands-free functionality, though she notes the hardware could be more durable.
Hailey - Black/Gold$1184.5(2580)Crystal R.Verified Buyer5.0I cannot say enough good about these products! I don’t even bother carrying a purse anymore, just my bandolier!Bridget W.Verified Buyer5.0Funny I got an invite to review Bandolier. Because I recently reviewed a competitor stating why I believe Bandolier is superior. I acknowledge that I tried to find a suitable Bandolier knockoff. Reality is that this brand is expensive. And although I love the product it has its flaws. The hardware could be a lot better. The clips break and they break with everyday use. But let me expand: I wear my phone on a strap all day everyday. I don’t carry my phone in my hand or use a bag. I wear my phone as a crossbody. I wear it while I get ready in the morning, when I cook, when I sit down to eat, when I’m walking, when I’m driving, when I’m working. My phone is always on my body. I only take it off for sleep and for showering. Ok-level set expectations. Given my constant wear, the clips tend to break. I’ve had 3 Badolier utility straps. The clips have broken on all 3. No replacement hardware and no offer from Bandolier to fix or replace. Ok. Next, the cell phone case fits snuggly. This is where the competitor lost. My phone simply fell out of the case when getting out of the car. I’ve purchased more than 9 bandolier phone cases over the years for 3 people over 3 different iPhone models (XS Max and 14 Pro Max and 17 Pro Max). Not once has a phone mistakenly fell out of the case. Hands down the best case I’ve had for a very expensive phone. With the 14 Pro Max I tripped on a curb in a parking lot and hit my hands, elbows, knees and face in concrete. The case got a bit banged up. But not a scratch on the phone. The case still worked after the pedestrian vs curb accident. The hardware didn’t even break. I, unfortunately, ended up with a torn ACL and broken wrist. I landed on my side and hip laying on top of my phone. I got a phone shaped bruise on the front of the hip from landing on the phone. But my phone survived. Like I said, I tried a competitor. I came back because I want peace of mind. I got the cool chrome finish trying to be more hip, only to find out that the finish peels and shows scratches. Remember I said I wear my phone and I need a case that can withstand my daily use. So I recently ordered the legacy black with gold hardware. No worry about pretend shiny metal that scratches/peels. The basic black case works for my needs. Would I like a pretty case-you bet. But it has to hold up to my demanding daily needs. I recommend Bandolier to anyone who asks about my crossbody strap and phone case. I threw the competitor case away because I didn’t want anyone else to experience the scare of the phone falling out of the case. Bandolier gave me such great peace of mind that I do not carry a purse unless I need to have more than my phone and basic ID and cards. I never leave the house without it. The phone case is as much a part of my life and daily routine as putting on clothes for the day. Thank you for making a product I can trust. Please work on better hardware - the gear is not cheap so at least offer options when the hardware breaks.Is Hailey available in other colors?What's the Hailey's standout feature?Can I see customer reviews for Hailey?Give us feedback
